      <data key="d12">function</data>
      <data key="d3">.github/scripts/summary.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">76</data>
      <data key="d14">97</data>
      <data key="d15">def git_short_sha(cwd: Path) -&gt; str | None:</data>
      <data key="d16">Best-effort `git rev-parse --short HEAD`. None on any failure -- not a
    git checkout, git missing, a timeout, or a non-zero exit.

    Follows the repo's git-subprocess-decoding rule (AGENTS.md): no
    text=True/encoding=, quotepath disabled, bytes decoded with
    surrogateescape, and a timeout that turns into a plain failure rather
    than a hang.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3509.03" y="0.00" width="123.05" height="29.90" />
