    <node id="sym:repo2graph/chunks.py::_lines">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/chunks.py::_lines</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_lines</data>
      <data key="d11">_lines</data>
      <data key="d12">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/chunks.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">17</data>
      <data key="d14">25</data>
      <data key="d15">def _lines(src: str) -&gt; list[str]:</data>
      <data key="d16">Split source the way tree-sitter counts rows: on "\\n" only.

    str.splitlines() also breaks on U+2028/U+2029/U+0085/\\x0b/\\x0c, which
    tree-sitter's row numbers do not; using it here slices every later symbol's
    chunk from the wrong lines (ISS-22). Drop a trailing "\\r" per line so
    CRLF files still index cleanly.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3524.12" y="516.40" width="66.00" height="28.60" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_lines</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:repo2graph/chunks.py::_keepends_lf">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/chunks.py::_keepends_lf</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">_keepends_lf</data>
      <data key="d11">_keepends_lf</data>
      <data key="d12">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/chunks.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">28</data>
      <data key="d14">40</data>
      <data key="d15">def _keepends_lf(text: str) -&gt; list[str]:</data>
      <data key="d16">Split on "\\n" only, keeping the newline, so "".join(result) == text.

    str.splitlines(keepends=True) also breaks on U+2028/U+2029/U+0085/\\x0b/\\x0c,
    which tree-sitter does not treat as row breaks; splitting a chunk there makes
    its pieces depend on whichever stray separators the source happens to hold
    (the ISS-22 bug class). Same "\\n"-only rule as _lines, but lossless.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="3614.12" y="516.40" width="112.50" height="29.25" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">_keepends_lf</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
