    <node id="sym:repo2graph/events.py::encodable">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/events.py::encodable</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">encodable</data>
      <data key="d11">encodable</data>
      <data key="d12">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/events.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">34</data>
      <data key="d14">75</data>
      <data key="d15">def encodable(text: str, stream: Any) -&gt; str:</data>
      <data key="d16">Return `text` reduced to something `stream` is guaranteed to accept.

    The stream's encoding and error handler are read at call time, not at import
    time: tests replace `sys.stdout` after import, and a caller may reconfigure
    it mid-run.

    Args:
        text: The text about to be written.
        stream: The destination stream, inspected for `.encoding`/`.errors`.

    Returns:
        `text` unchanged when the stream can represent it, otherwise the same
        text with unrepresentable characters replaced.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1816.25" y="694.40" width="98.75" height="32.50" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">encodable</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
    <node id="sym:repo2graph/events.py::write_safe">
      <data key="d0">sym:repo2graph/events.py::write_safe</data>
      <data key="d1">symbol</data>
      <data key="d2">write_safe</data>
      <data key="d11">write_safe</data>
      <data key="d12">function</data>
      <data key="d3">repo2graph/events.py</data>
      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">78</data>
      <data key="d14">105</data>
      <data key="d15">def write_safe(stream: Any, text: str, newline: str = "\n") -&gt; None:</data>
      <data key="d16">Write `text` to `stream`, replacing anything it cannot encode.

    Never raises: a UnicodeEncodeError, a closed stream or a broken pipe all end
    as silence rather than as an exception in the caller.

    Args:
        stream: Destination, typically `sys.stdout` or `sys.stderr`.
        text: The line to write, without a trailing newline.
        newline: Appended to `text`; pass "" to suppress it.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1939.00" y="694.40" width="133.30" height="40.30" />
          <y:Fill color="#57C7E3" transparent="false" />
          <y:BorderStyle color="#4a4f57" type="line" width="1.0" />
          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" fontSize="11" textColor="#1c2330" visible="true">write_safe</y:NodeLabel>
          <y:Shape type="ellipse" />
        </y:ShapeNode>
      </data>
    </node>
