      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">348</data>
      <data key="d14">381</data>
      <data key="d15">def _read_and_parse(item):</data>
      <data key="d16">Read one file and parse it if it is code.

    Top level, and returns only counts plus the ParsedFile, so a process pool
    can pickle both the call and its result. The fourth element of the read
    tuple is the sha256 of the bytes just parsed: it is computed here because
    this is the only place that holds them, and build() never keeps them.</data>
