      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">393</data>
      <data key="d14">422</data>
      <data key="d15">def cache_entry(lang: str | None, size: int, lines: int, pf, digest: str) -&gt; dict:</data>
      <data key="d16">Serialise one file's parse result for `parse.cache.json`.

    Args:
        lang: Language id the file was parsed as, or None for a non-code file.
        size: Length in bytes of the file as indexed.
        lines: Newline count + 1, as recorded on the file node.
        pf: The `ParsedFile` for this file, or None if it was not parsed.
        digest: sha256 hex digest of the bytes this entry describes.

    Returns:
        A JSON-serialisable dict holding everything `build()` needs to rebuild
        this file's nodes and edges without re-reading or re-parsing it.</data>
      <data key="d4">
        <y:ShapeNode>
          <y:Geometry x="1845.55" y="872.40" width="104.62" height="29.25" />
