      <data key="d5">python</data>
      <data key="d13">343</data>
      <data key="d14">359</data>
      <data key="d15">def test_async_build_is_off_by_default(mini_repo, monkeypatch):</data>
      <data key="d16">The synchronous build is a considered default, not an oversight.

    A build that outlives its client still writes a real index to disk, so the
    retry is instant -- a failure that heals itself. --async-build exists for
    the case that reasoning does not cover: a very large repo behind a client
    whose tool-call timeout no single build can fit inside.</data>
      <data key="d17">true</data>
